<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- THE LAUNCHER ICON (the manifest's android:icon; the launcher and the
     recents card). It is the Linux one: Breeze's audio-x-generic, the
     packaging/warptempo_gui.desktop's Icon=, vendored verbatim as
     assets/icons/breeze/audio-x-generic.svg (the 64 px mimetype rendition).
     An ADAPTIVE icon, the whole of it: minSdk is 30, so no legacy
     ic_launcher.png set exists beside it.

     Two layers per density under res/mipmap-<density>/:
       ic_launcher_background.png  solid opaque #292C30, the row ground
                                   kRedesignRowGround (src/gui/render.h), the
                                   colour the tablet's status bar wears, so the
                                   launcher's mask is filled with the app's
                                   chrome colour;
       ic_launcher_foreground.png  the glyph, RGBA, on a transparent surround.

     THE 58-OF-108 RULE. The adaptive canvas is 108 dp and only its central
     66 dp circle is guaranteed visible under every mask (circle, squircle,
     rounded square: the launcher's choice). The SVG's 64-unit document is
     scaled to 58 dp and centred on the canvas (25 dp each side): the sheet,
     50 units wide, spans about 45 dp, whose diagonal (about 64 dp) is within
     the 66 dp circle, and the disc's rim, 29 units from the document's
     centre, lands about 26 dp out, inside the 33 dp radius. (The sheet sits
     2 units left of the document's centre, so its two left corners reach
     about 33.4 dp: on the safe circle's edge, and inside the 36 dp radius of
     the 72 dp viewport every mask is drawn within.) The glyph's own
     visual centre, (33, 32) in its 64 units, is near enough the document's
     that no offset is taken. At density factor f (mdpi 1, hdpi 1.5, xhdpi 2,
     xxhdpi 3, xxxhdpi 4) the canvas is 108·f px and the glyph 58·f px, both
     whole; the page offset (108·f − 58·f) / 2 is 37.5 at hdpi, which
     rsvg-convert places exactly (antialiased) instead of flooring it.

     A ONE-SHOT, NOT A BUILD STEP: the PNGs are rendered once on the laptop and
     committed; a retouch is a re-run of this recipe, never a build step
     (build_apk.sh only compiles res/). The recipe, from the repo root
     (rsvg-convert 2.62, ImageMagick 7), for each density n at factor f with
     C = 108·f, G = 58·f, O = (C − G) / 2:

       mdpi     C=108 G=58  O=25      hdpi    C=162 G=87  O=37.5
       xhdpi    C=216 G=116 O=50      xxhdpi  C=324 G=174 O=75
       xxxhdpi  C=432 G=232 O=100

       rsvg-convert -w G -h G \
           - -page-width C - -page-height C - -left O - -top O \
           assets/icons/breeze/audio-x-generic.svg -o fg.png
       magick fg.png -strip -define png:compression-level=9 \
           -define png:compression-filter=5 \
           PNG32:android/app/res/mipmap-n/ic_launcher_foreground.png
       magick -size CxC xc:'#292C30' -strip \
           PNG8:android/app/res/mipmap-n/ic_launcher_background.png

     (The long options are spelt "- -" above only because an XML comment may
     not hold two adjacent hyphens: type them as the usual double hyphen.)
     The foreground stays RGBA: a palette encoding of it is not lossless (its
     antialiased alpha edges), while the one-colour background is. -->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_background"/>
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground"/>
</adaptive-icon>
